# Agent reporting format (always-on)

Every **end-of-task summary, progress update, investigation answer, and clarifying question** uses the same shape, regardless of model. Full spec and real examples: **`agent-reporting`** skill (`.agent/skills/agent-reporting/SKILL.md`).

**Scope:** Cursor and Claude Code. **OpenCode is exempt** (its output is already the reference). Never add this rule to `opencode.json` `instructions` or to `AGENTS.md`.

## Skeleton

```
<one-line outcome>

## <Section>
<tight bullets, table, or 1-2 sentences>

## Verification
<gates actually run, with results>

<one closing question or single next action>
```

| Element    | Rule                                                                  |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| First line | Plain sentence, **no heading**, says what happened. PR/URL goes here. |
| Sections   | `##` only, **max 5**, titles of 1 to 3 words. Drop empty ones.        |
| Bullets    | One line each, subject first, **one nesting level max**               |
| Closing    | Exactly one question or one next action                               |

Target under ~150 words for a small change, ~400 for a module.

## Report types (pick one, do not blend)

| Type           | Sections                                                    |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Implementation | What changed · Verification · Docs · Notes                  |
| Investigation  | Short answer · What is happening · Options · Recommendation |
| Deploy         | Shipped · Verification · Cleanup                            |
| Blocked        | What works · What is blocked · Next step                    |
| Mid-task       | No sections. One or two lines, then keep working.           |

## Emphasis carries the color

`**bold**` = the outcome word, a status, a count, a PR link, the one risky detail (one per bullet). `` `code` `` = paths, commands, identifiers, statuses, branches, env vars. Tables for before/after and gate/result.

## Fixed status words

`pass` · `fail` · `skipped` · `not run` · `blocked` · `N/A — <why>`

Never claim a gate you did not run. Never report a result you did not read.

## Always state what you did not do

Uncommitted files and why · gates skipped · pre-existing failures you did not cause · anything needing **`kamewave`** (never offered as a casual next step) · `Plans/RBAC: N/A — <why>` and `activity-log: N/A — <why>` when they do not apply.

## Questions

**One** decision per message, last in the message, recommended option first and labeled `(recommended)`. Prefer the `AskQuestion` tool in Cursor. Never ask what the code or docs already answer.

## Banned

Opening heading · `## Summary` / `## Overview` / `## Conclusion` · preamble ("I've completed", "Great!") · em dash `—` · decorative emoji or ✅/❌ as status · numbered mega-outlines · "Let me know if you need anything else" · narrating tool calls · self-criticism and apologies · claiming done when a gate failed.

